<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Roosevelt returns for his yearly preventive visit, five weeks after his six-month asthma review. He has had no further exacerbations since the August cold, no night waking, and uses one reliever inhalation before boxing or rowing and rarely otherwise. He trains five days a week. He has no new concerns. He reports good adherence to his maintenance inhaler and keeps a weekly peak-flow record in the green zone. His last eye examination was more than two years ago and his glasses feel weaker for distance. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic preventive visit, age 23</td></tr><tr><td>Asthma since last visit</td><td>No exacerbations; reliever before exercise only; peak flow in the green zone</td></tr><tr><td>Vision</td><td>Distance glasses feel weaker; last eye examination more than two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Budesonide-formoterol maintenance and as needed; no other medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No injuries, emergency visits, or hospital stays</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Boxing three times a week, rowing, and long weekend hill walks; more than 300 minutes of activity a week</td></tr><tr><td>Diet</td><td>Large appetite; mixed diet with fruit and vegetables most days</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco and nicotine</td><td>Never smoked or vaped; avoids smoky rooms</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>Rare alcohol (AUDIT-C 1); no drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six to seven hours on session nights; no snoring or daytime sleepiness</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy and engaged at work; good friendships; no loneliness</td></tr><tr><td>Injury and safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; uses headgear and a mouthguard when sparring; no firearms at home</td></tr><tr><td>Sun exposure</td><td>Long hours outdoors on hill walks and on the water; rarely uses sunscreen</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>One partner; no concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

