    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Healthy young adult. Depression and alcohol screens are negative, and his blood pressure is normal. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Moderate persistent asthma, well controlled (J45.40)</content>. No symptoms apart from planned pre-exercise reliever use since recovering from the August exacerbation. [S]<list><item>Continue maintenance-and-reliever therapy; step-down will be considered at the next asthma review if he stays controlled with no exacerbations.</item><item>Influenza vaccine today.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Myopia, both eyes (H52.13)</content>. Distance acuity 20/40 with current glasses suggests an outdated prescription. [S]<list><item>Refer to optometry for refraction and new glasses.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Sun exposure</content>. Fair skin and many hours outdoors without sun protection. [S]<list><item>Counseling on broad-spectrum sunscreen, a hat, and protective clothing.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today; recommended every year, and especially with asthma</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed under current CDC guidance for adults with chronic lung disease; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 given at his four-week asthma review for chronic lung disease; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven years ago; next booster due in three years</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed in adolescence</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco or nicotine; advised to keep avoiding smoke, a key asthma trigger</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/70 mmHg; recheck every three to five years</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with his consent; no prior result on record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer prevention counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Recommended for fair-skinned people up to age 24; sun protection advice given</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Referred</td><td>Optometry referral for refraction</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid and diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No risk factors; diabetes screening starts at 35 for adults with overweight or obesity</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker, and below the screening ages</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV and hepatitis C tests with his next blood draw. Optometry referral. Asthma review in about three months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
